Educational Roadmap

Dual Enrollment at Austin Community College (ACC):

Starting in 9th grade, the team will enroll in ACC courses to gain early college credits and foundational knowledge for MIT.

MIT Goals:

Venice Showels (Project Lead):

Course 16 (Aeronautics and Astronautics)
Focus: Plasma propulsion, nuclear fusion reactors, and ship engineering.
Goal: Build the engines and propulsion systems required for interstellar spacecraft.
Potential Air Force Base Placement: California or Ohio (propulsion and engine focus).
Eli Stinson (Aerodynamics and Astrophysics Lead):

Course 8/16 (Physics and Aerospace Focus)
Focus: Astrophysics, studying stars, black holes, and quantum dynamics.
Goal: Provide the theoretical and practical knowledge necessary for space exploration.
Potential Air Force Base Placement: Space-focused research hubs in California, Ohio, or astrophysics data centers.
Christian Lockett (Systems Integration and IT Lead):

Course 6 (Computer Science and Electrical Engineering)
Focus: Software and hardware engineering, IT systems integration, AI control systems.
Goal: Develop AI systems to power spacecraft and their infrastructure.
Potential Air Force Base Placement: California or technology/IT hubs in the Air Force.
AFROTC Program:

Participate in MIT’s ROTC program to gain discipline, leadership skills, and zero student debt.
Focus on Air Force roles that align with your technical expertise:
Engine design, propulsion systems, astrophysics data, or IT infrastructure.
Steps to Achieve Goals

Short-Term:

Begin ACC coursework in 9th grade that aligns with your MIT goals (e.g., physics, engineering, programming).
Collaborate as SSL PRIME to build early plasma propulsion models and simulations.
Use GitHub to manage projects and maintain code for AI and physics systems.
Medium-Term:

Attend MIT and finish programs at an accelerated pace (4 years).
Graduate with expertise in plasma propulsion, astrophysics, and IT systems integration.
Serve in ROTC and Air Force roles that provide experience in aerospace systems and global operations.
Long-Term:

Found SSL PRIME as a sustainable engineering company focused on Earth’s transportation systems.
Expand into interstellar propulsion research and commercial spacecraft systems.
Achieve interstellar space travel capabilities within your lifetime (goal: Alpha Centauri in 40 years).
